      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That pattern you're observing is likely an example of the reverse psychological effect known as self-fulfilling prophecy, where your focus or controlled breathing subconsciously influences real-time choices made by others, causing market movements to align with your internal state rather than your body leading the action. If your heart truly dictates algorithmic price changes, the market would lack its typical competitive edge, whereas usually, the trader's psychological state precedes any observable change in the data stream. To confirm whether this is a genuine feedback loop, you would need to experiment by tracing these patterns during live, unedited news events versus structured algorithmic drafts to see if the reaction is primary to the event or a symptom of your cognitive engagement with it. Ultimately, stating that your heart rate directly controls the market is a phenomenon more commonly associated with the \"synchronicity\" seen in high-level psychological settings than in stochastic environments.",
